  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">for support of the African Feminist Forum</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As a Pan-African feminist funder, the African Women&#x2019;s Development Fund (AWDF) plays a critical and unique role within African feminist movements to fund, strengthen, and elevate groups led by African feminists, women, girls, and gender-diverse people working toward gender justice and social transformation. Through a deepened movement-building and intersectional approach, AWDF has evolved how it resources, supports, and nurtures African feminist movements with an expansion of core funding and responsive accompaniment. With this grant, AWDF will revitalize collective African feminist solidarity, community, and voice by reconvening the African Feminist Forum and reviving national and regional African feminist forums and structures. (Gender Equity and Governance)</narrative>
  </description>
